  "reasons": {
    "graphql": "GraphQL plumbing: the shared authentication and permission examples (requires current user/organization/permission) and the GraphQL type definitions. Tanvo serves Connect RPCs; authentication and permissions are libs/auth's, tested there, and the request and response shapes are the protos of libs/proto.",
    "premium": "Premium license and premium integration gates. Tanvo has no premium gates: every integration is available (parity §1.50).",
    "nango": "Behavior of the Nango aggregator that Tanvo does not have: Tanvo calls each vendor's API directly, so there is no connection_id, Nango sync, account information, restlet endpoint, cursor parameter or Nango task and memory error (parity §1.37): connection_id is Nango's (models/integrations/*_integration.rb validates it), PerformSyncJob and SendRestletEndpointJob drive Nango (netsuite/create_service.rb:38-42), and the out of memory, task and orchestrator errors are Nango function failures (aggregator/base_service.rb:8-21).",
    "contention": "Kept deviation: a 5xx from the vendor is treated as server contention and retried by the job (apiclient retries, then the job's backoff), where the upstream returns the action_script_runtime_error failure of a Nango script. With a direct API a 5xx is the vendor's transient failure, not a script error.",
    "rails": "Rails and ActiveRecord mechanics with no Go counterpart: associations, paper_trail, the settings and secrets JSON accessors (Tanvo stores typed columns, tested through the services' stored values), single-table-inheritance scopes and customer_type, memoization, class factories (Tanvo dispatches on the provider with a typed interface, so an unsupported provider cannot be built), job lock keys, and a stubbed update! raising RecordInvalid (the company ID write has no model validation to fail).",
    "planned": "The connection code of integration customers and billing objects routed to a connection are planned parity rows owned outside this module (parity §1.37 connection codes); their cases are ported with that work.",
    "one-api": "Kept deviation: one Connect RPC (UpsertConnection) serves the REST and dashboard clients, keyed by customer and integration, so there is no missing connection to report and the provider sync is enqueued as in create_or_update_batch_service.rb:48-60 rather than called synchronously as in netsuite_service.rb:22-23.",
    "unreachable": "Code with no caller in the upstream application: the query paths without an integration (the resolvers require integration_id), HubSpot call_async services, the HubSpot companies and contacts object type ID helpers (hubspot_integration.rb:14-20) and the fee.tax_provider_error webhook (nothing enqueues it; send_webhook_job.rb:35 is only the mapping).",
    "ids": "Tanvo fees always carry UUIDv7 IDs, previews included (fees/service.go), so there is no fee without an ID and the ID order is the generation order.",
    "email": "The document job carries no notify flag: libs/mail decides from the billing entity's email settings (libs/mail/documents.go), with no premium gate.",
    "segment": "Segment product analytics (SegmentTrackJob): the core sends no product analytics, as for the other Segment calls (docs/parity.md, catalog cache row).",
    "map": "The proto map of currency mappings cannot hold a duplicate currency, so the duplicate error cannot be produced.",
    "auth": "Okta integrations belong to libs/auth and are tested there.",
    "legacy_script": "Accessor of NetSuite's legacy_script setting, which no service, mutation or API of v1.55.0 sets (declared at app/models/integrations/netsuite_integration.rb:8 and read only at app/services/integrations/aggregator/contacts/payloads/netsuite.rb:72), so every integration has it false; Tanvo has no such setting and behaves as false (providers/netsuite ports the false cases)."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Kept deviations ported with their own expectations: HubSpot and Xero requests are throttled per connection, as both vendors limit per account or tenant (the upstream throttles them globally, config/initializers/throttling.rb), and Xero's daily limit is left to the 429 retry; payload IDs drop the lago_ prefix (customer_id, integration_id)."
  ],
